            <ArticleTitle>Local anesthetic switching for intrathecal tachyphylaxis in cancer patients with pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>187-9, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Switching from bupivacaine to lidocaine may improve intrathecal morphine analgesia in advanced cancer patients, possibly because of different spinal mechanisms limiting the hyperalgesic processes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
